{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - Phase A: Initial review of C1 remaining work scope\n   - Phase B: Codex agent driver design initiation (deferred by review)\n   - Phase C: Complete atoll up + home model implementation via review-driven iteration\n   - Phase D: Establish permanent division of labor: codex exec for all code fixes, human for review/verify/collect only\n   - Current: Summary generation with zero tool calls\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - **home model architecture**: ~/.atoll/{server,device} structure; one PC=one daemon; one live process enforced via homelock flock; identity=credential ownership\n   - **device identity triple**: {daemon_id, api_key, server_ws}; immutable until rebind; persist-then-commit pattern for durability\n   - **token rotation strategy**: BootstrapOwnerToken atomically replaces session on EVERY boot (not just --init); fallback for leaked credentials=restart\n   - **engineboot assembly**: Four public API doors only (ProvisionLocalNode, RotateOwnerToken, Serve, Close); Ready/BoundAddr threading contract; graceful shutdown order (HTTP drain → gateway close → realm workers → db close)\n   - **homelock enforcement**: Exclusive flock on <home>/.lock prevents double-process accidents; EWOULDBLOCK → human-readable error\n   - **review-driven fix discipline**: Six rounds identified cascading issues; root causes: site enumeration (拍点=全称命题), verification depth variance, assumption contradictions\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **cmd/atoll/main.go**: supervisor with triple lockfile (serverHome/channelDir/deviceHome); homelock Acquire; initDB rollbackTargets precise snapshot; failNode closure; persistClaim persist-then-commit; provision partial result contract; device goroutine Ready sync\n   - **cmd/daemon/main.go**: -